```lean
theorem perelmanF_step_le (F : ReactionField ι) {c : ι → ℝ} (hc : ∀ i, 1 ≤ c i)
    {h : ℝ} (hh : 0 ≤ h) {traj : ℕ → ι → ℝ} (ev : DiscreteEvolution F h traj) (n : ℕ) :
    perelmanF c (traj (n + 1)) ≤ perelmanF c (traj n) := by
  unfold perelmanF
  refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun i _ => ?_
  rw [ev.step n i]
  exact gibbsTerm_step_le (hc i) (mul_nonneg hh (F.eval_nonneg (traj n) i))
```

Full antitonicity:
```lean
theorem perelmanF_antitone_discrete (F) (hc) (hh) (ev) :
    ∀ ⦃m n : ℕ⦄, m ≤ n → perelmanF c (traj n) ≤ perelmanF c (traj m) := by
  intro m n hmn
  induction n, hmn using Nat.le_induction with
  | base => exact le_rfl
  | succ n hmn ih => exact (perelmanF_step_le F hc hh ev n).trans ih
```
Wait, `Nat.le_induction` with `m ≤ n`: the induction step from `m ≤ n` to `m ≤ n+1` gives `perelmanF (traj (n+1)) ≤ perelmanF (traj n) ≤ perelmanF (traj m)`. Good.

